  <section class="faq-section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading"><div class="container"><div class="faq-layout"><div><div class="section-label">Common Questions</div><h2 class="section-title" id="faq-heading">Carson Mortgage FAQs</h2><p class="section-sub" style="margin-bottom:2rem;">Answers to the questions I hear most from buyers in Carson.</p><div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Is Carson a good place to buy in the South Bay?<span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></button><div class="faq-answer"><p>For buyers who want genuine value — a full-sized SFR on a real lot, good schools, and easy access to the South Bay employment corridor — Carson is one of the best options available at the $700K–$900K price range. At $800K median, you typically get significantly more square footage and lot size than you would in Torrance, Redondo Beach, or Hawthorne at the same price.</p></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">What are Carson schools like?<span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></button><div class="faq-answer"><p>Carson is served by Los Angeles Unified School District. The standout is the California Academy of Math & Science (CAMS) — a magnet high school in north Carson (90746) that consistently ranks among the top public high schools in California. Carson High School also serves the city. School quality is a primary driver of demand in the 90746 zip code specifically.</p></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Which Carson zip code is better — 90745 or 90746?<span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></button><div class="faq-answer"><p>90746 (north Carson) is generally considered more desirable and commands higher prices — bordered by Gardena and Torrance, served by CAMS, and featuring more recent construction. 90745 (south Carson) offers more accessible prices, especially for FHA buyers, with larger lots and strong rental demand from proximity to the port and employment corridors. Which is right for you depends on your budget and priorities.</p></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can I use an FHA loan to buy in Carson?<span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></button><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes — FHA loans are one of the most effective programs in Carson, especially in 90745. With a city median around $800K and many properties in the $650K–$850K range, FHA financing with 3.5% down is accessible for most first-time buyers. I can verify FHA eligibility for any specific property in a single call.</p></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">I'm buying an investment property in Carson. What loans are available?<span class="faq-chevron">▼</span></button><div class="faq-answer"><p>DSCR loans are commonly used by investors in Carson — they qualify based on rental income rather than your personal income or tax returns. Carson has strong rental demand from port workers, logistics employees, and South Bay commuters, making it an active investment market. I can show you how a DSCR deal is structured in a 20-minute conversation.</p></div></div></div></div><div><div class="faq-cta-card"><h3>Still Have Questions?</h3><p>Call me for straight answers about Carson financing. Real numbers, no scripts.</p><ul class="faq-cta-list"><li>Free, no-obligation consultation</li><li>FHA through jumbo — all programs</li><li>Self-employed &amp; complex income welcome</li><li>Same-day response</li><li>NMLS# 999113 — licensed in CA</li></ul><a href="tel:+13105945362" style="display:block;background:var(--gold);color:var(--navy-deep);text-align:center;padding:0.9rem 1.5rem;border-radius:8px;font-weight:700;font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">📞 Call (310) 594-5362</a><a href="https://www.rudycorona.com/contact" style="display:block;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.1);color:#fff;border:1.5px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.3);text-align:center;paddin